{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"55073","self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/55073","key":"SV-8939","renderedFields":{"statuscategorychangedate":"Today 10:27 AM","issuetype":null,"timespent":null,"project":null,"customfield_10351":"","fixVersions":null,"aggregatetimespent":null,"statusCategory":null,"resolution":null,"resolutiondate":null,"workratio":null,"watches":null,"issuerestriction":null,"lastViewed":null,"created":"Today 10:27 AM","customfield_10021":null,"customfield_10385":null,"priority":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10016":null,"customfield_10019":null,"timeestimate":null,"aggregatetimeoriginalestimate":null,"versions":null,"customfield_10418":null,"customfield_10419":null,"issuelinks":null,"assignee":null,"updated":"Today 10:27 AM","status":null,"components":null,"timeoriginalestimate":null,"description":"<h3><a name=\"1.Whathappensnow\"></a>1. What happens now</h3>\n\n<p>The Parts Velocity report opens with its Location filter set to <b>All locations</b>, so the first thing a user sees is every location they have access to, mixed together. The written description asks it to open on the one location the user is actually working in.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"2.Whatshouldhappeninstead\"></a>2. What should happen instead</h3>\n\n<p>Parts Velocity specification, version 5, requirement S2-R9: \"The toolbar provides a Location multi-select filter as the rightmost control in the filter row... On a first visit it defaults to the user's currently active location (the location currently selected in the application's global location switcher).\"</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"3.Howtoseeit\"></a>3. How to see it</h3>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Sign in as a user who has access to more than one location. Check the location shown beside your name at the top right - it reads <b>Staging Heavy Duty - 9919</b>.</li>\n\t<li>Open <b>Reports</b> &gt; <b>Parts Velocity</b> for the first time in this browser.</li>\n\t<li>Read the Location filter at the right-hand end of the filter row, and read the Location column in the table.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p><b>Exact test data this was seen with:</b> organisation <b>Staging Foothills Group Inc</b>; the signed-in user's active location <b>Staging Heavy Duty - 9919</b>; the other accessible location <b>Staging Lethbridge - 4310</b>. This was a genuine first visit - the browser had no saved view for this report.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"4.Whatwasactuallyshown\"></a>4. What was actually shown</h3>\n\n<p>The filter read <b>All locations</b>, and the table returned rows from both locations - for example <b>BRAKECLEAN</b> appeared once for <b>Staging Heavy Duty - 9919</b> and again for <b>Staging Lethbridge - 4310</b>.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"5.Whatwasruledout\"></a>5. What was ruled out</h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><b>It is not a remembered setting from an earlier visit.</b> The browser was brand new and held no saved view for this report; the very first request the page sent carried no location at all, and the second carried both.</li>\n\t<li><b>It is not the filter being broken.</b> Choosing a single location works correctly and narrows the report - it is only the starting value that is wrong.</li>\n\t<li><b>It is not a permissions question.</b> Both locations are ones this user is allowed to see.</li>\n\t<li><b>Note for triage:</b> the same starting behaviour was reported on Inventory Value as \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro\" data-jira-key=\"SV-8931\" >\n                <a href=\"https://shopview.atlassian.net/browse/SV-8931\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Inventory Value opens on All locations instead of the user&#39;s current location\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10854?size=medium\" />\n            SV-8931\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-complete jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Open</span>\n            </span>\n. This ticket is the Parts Velocity report, which has its own requirement wording.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h3><a name=\"6.Howoften\"></a>6. How often</h3>\n\n<p>Every time. Seen on every fresh browser session opened during this test.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"7.Whereitwasseen\"></a>7. Where it was seen</h3>\n\n<p>Reports &gt; Parts Velocity, on the QA branch, build v3.5-16cf83f, on 6 August 2026.</p>","customfield_10015":null,"timetracking":{},"security":null,"aggregatetimeestimate":null,"attachment":[],"summary":null,"creator":null,"subtasks":null,"customfield_10285":"","reporter":null,"customfield_10044":null,"aggregateprogress":null,"customfield_10046":null,"customfield_10047":null,"environment":"","customfield_10318":null,"duedate":null,"customfield_10518":null,"progress":null,"votes":null,"comment":{"comments":[],"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/55073/comment","maxResults":0,"total":0,"startAt":0},"worklog":{"startAt":0,"maxResults":20,"total":0,"worklogs":[]}},"fields":{"statuscategorychangedate":"2026-08-06T00:27:28.885-0500","issuetype":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issuetype/10007","id":"10007","description":"Subtasks track small pieces of work that are part of a larger task. (Migrated on 31 Dec 2023 09:01 UTC)","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10854?size=medium","name":"Story Defect","subtask":true,"avatarId":10854,"entityId":"0900502c-ae66-465f-a9da-8322307b07ff","hierarchyLevel":-1},"parent":{"id":"54663","key":"SV-8642","self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/54663","fields":{"summary":"Velocity - Story 2 - Filters & Search","status":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/status/10349","description":"","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/","name":"Open","id":"10349","statusCategory":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/statuscategory/